The automorphisms:
- Fix {0, 1, -1}
- Can permute the positive reals (≠ 0, 1) in a very flexible way (any Q-linear automorphism of the multiplicative group (0,∞) \ {1}, or more precisely, any Q-linear automorphism of (R,+) that fixes 0)

So the orbits of the automorphism group on R are:
- {0}
- {1}
- {-1}
- (0, ∞) \ {1} (all positive reals except 1)
- (-∞, 0) \ {-1} (all negative reals except -1)

The orbits under Aut(R, *):
- Orbit of 0: {0} (fixed by all automorphisms)
- Orbit of 1: {1} (fixed by all automorphisms)
- Orbit of -1: {-1} (fixed by all automorphisms)
- Orbit of a for a > 0, a ≠ 1: I claimed this is all of (0, ∞) \ {1}
- Orbit of a for a < 0, a ≠ -1: I claimed this is all of (-∞, 0) \ {-1}
